CloudBurrow patch 110 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1522). Applies after patch 0102; needs
googlesqlite patches 0036 and 0074.

The bug: patch 0102 runs a jobs.query or query jobs.insert of one SELECT
statement as a read, without the write lock, beside the request that
holds it. A statement that names a change table ("$changes": the front's
APPENDS, CHANGES, time travel and history reads) first settles the
change table's pending records (googlesqlite patch 0074), which writes:
when another statement committed after the read's snapshot began, the
settling failed "database is locked". The front lets go of the history a
shorter time travel window let go (ALTER SCHEMA, datasets.patch) by
counting it first with such a read, and took the failure for nothing to
let go, so APPENDS and CHANGES read changes from before the window
(TestBigQueryAlterSchemaTimeTravelLetsGoFirst, main CI's emulators shard,
3 of 4 runs, whenever another job wrote at that moment).

The patch: a query that names a change table is not a read; it takes the
write lock as any other write does. TestChangeTableReadsBesideAWriter
reads a change table with pending records 40 times beside two INSERT
loops: without the patch every read fails "database is locked" (3 runs
of 3), with it every read answers.

